                "text_phbdHe": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<h3>Brady O’Connor, President</h3><p>Brady O’Connor most recently served as the Chief of External Affairs for the FIFA World Cup 26 New York New Jersey Host Committee. Brady’s responsibilities include supporting outreach & stakeholder engagement, intergovernmental affairs coordination, external stakeholder communications, and collaborating with the Commercial Program to reach commercial and fundraising goals, including managing the Host Committee Donor Program. </p><p>Before joining the Host Committee, Brady served as the Chief of Staff to the President & CEO of Choose New Jersey, the State’s leading marketing & business attraction non-profit, where he was responsible for supporting the CEO, managing external stakeholder communications, and leading the coordination of cross-departmental operations, including domestic and international trade and business development missions.</p><p>Prior to joining Choose New Jersey, Brady served as the Special Assistant to Governor Phil Murphy for the Governor’s first term, notably working on the FIFA World Cup 26 New York New Jersey bid committee.</p><p>A lifelong soccer fan, Brady received a Bachelor of Arts in Environmental Studies with a minor in Public Policy from Ramapo College of New Jersey where he currently serves on the Board of Trustees and played on the Men's Soccer team. Brady lives in Parsippany with his wife, Paulina, daughter, and their dog.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
